{
  "age_65plus_composition": "dynamic: 2030-2050 65+ curves recomposed from 65-74/75-84/85+ curves, each scaled by its own WCDE death-rate trend and weighted by its projected share of 65+ (baseline_heat_subband_ljubljana.csv)",
  "reference_year": 2020,
  "years": [
    2020,
    2030,
    2040,
    2050
  ],
  "scaling_source": "Masselot et al. (2023) Lancet Planet Health, Zenodo 10288665; future years use existing NB04 baseline_heat_scaling_{city}.csv ratios",
  "tail_mode": "loglinear",
  "notes": "Age-differentiated RR curves reconstructed from coefs.csv B-spline + city/age-specific Masselot MMT. No p99 rescaling and no 20C threshold. RR curves are converted to heat attributable fractions, AF=(RR-1)/RR, then to CLIMADA mdd using Masselot city-age annual death rates. Aggregated to URBADAPT bins via population-weighted per-person mdd. <15 set to zero; 15-64 approximated with Masselot 20-64. 2030/2040/2050 multiply the 2020 Masselot level by existing NB04 relative baseline-mortality scaling (for 65+ see age_65plus_composition). Log-linear tail extrapolation beyond historical tmax: log_rr extended using nonneg-constrained last-1C slope, converted through AF=(RR-1)/RR. ",
